# The fork's changes to the code of Z-Push 2.7.7 (tools/patch_source.py; the
# format and its rules are described there). setup/zpush.sh applies them to
# a fresh copy of Z-Push in a directory of root's own, before it moves the
# tree to /usr/local/lib/z-push, and stops if one does not apply. Each change
# names its bug in BUGS-fork.md with a "MIAB-Bnnn" comment. The installed
# tree is marked with Z-Push's version and a checksum of the blocks of this
# file (/usr/local/lib/z-push/version, "2.7.7+patches-<16 hex digits>",
# tools/patch_source.py --digest; comments and empty lines outside the
# blocks do not change it): when a block changes, or the installed tree no
# longer has every change (a file changed by hand), setup installs a fresh
# copy from GitHub on every box, so a block is always applied to the
# original text and may be edited. Z-Push's configuration
# (config.php, the backends' config.php) is not changed here: setup sets it
# on every run.

# B126: the logs that the miab-zpush jail reads. Z-Push writes text that a
# client chooses (the user name of the Authorization header, the e-mail
# address of an autodiscover request) unescaped into its logs. Each line
# starts with the user names in brackets ("[<user>]", or
# "[<user>#<user of the URL>]"), as the client sent them: with a "]" in them
# the jail's filter could not tell where the brackets end, and a warning that
# ends in text from a client could pass for a failed login with any address.
# Escape "]" and "\" there (as "\]" and "\\"), so that the first unescaped
# "]" ends the user names; the filter requires the message that follows to be
# the failed login of that same user. No other unescaped copy of these
# prefixes may be left.

@@ lib/log/filelog.php
<<<
            if (strcasecmp($this->GetAuthUser(), $this->GetUser()) == 0) {
                $log .= ' ['. $this->GetUser() .']';
            }
            else {
                $log .= ' ['. $this->GetAuthUser() . Request::IMPERSONATE_DELIM . $this->GetUser() .']';
            }
===
            if (strcasecmp($this->GetAuthUser(), $this->GetUser()) == 0) {
                $log .= ' ['. addcslashes($this->GetUser(), '\\]') .']'; // MIAB-B126: the user names escaped
            }
            else {
                $log .= ' ['. addcslashes($this->GetAuthUser() . Request::IMPERSONATE_DELIM . $this->GetUser(), '\\]') .']'; // MIAB-B126: the user names escaped
            }
>>>

