# B126: Z-Push logged a failed ActiveSync login as "[<user>] IP: <address>
# failed to authenticate user '<user>'": text that the client chooses on both
# sides of the address, so no filter can tell which address Z-Push wrote. Put
# the address last, as in the autodiscover message, where the jail's filter
# anchors it at the end of the line. Only the format string changes: its
# arguments stay the same, in their positions (%1$s, %2$s). Z-Push also wrote
# that line for a request without a password (with the user name of the URL,
# "User=", or "unknown"): a phone sends its first request without credentials
# and waits for the login prompt, so each sync of a phone would count as a
# failed login. Write it only when the request had a user name and a
# password, i.e. when Z-Push checked a password.

@@ index.php
