# B126: a login that fails because Dovecot or Nextcloud cannot check the
# password at that moment (Dovecot answers "[UNAVAILABLE] Temporary
# authentication failure" while users.sqlite is locked, closes the
# connection, or does not run) is no wrong password, but Z-Push reported it as
# one: HTTP 401, which makes a phone ask for its password, and the failed-login
# line that the miab-zpush jail counts. Every user behind one address (a NAT,
# or the few relays of the Outlook app) could be banned so in such a window.
# Z-Push answers it with 503 and Retry-After instead, which a client retries
# later, and logs no failed login. A wrong password is what Dovecot answers
# with "[AUTHENTICATIONFAILED]" (on any of c-client's tries); any other IMAP
# failure is temporary. When IMAP accepted the password, a failed CalDAV or
# CardDAV login (Nextcloud) is temporary too.

@@ backend/imap/imap.php
